   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "כֵּיצַד מוֹשְׁחָן? כְּמִין כִּי, וְהַשְּׁאָר נֶאֱכָל וְכוּ׳. מַאי ״כְּמִין כִּי״? אָמַר רַב כָּהֲנָא: כְּמִין כִּי יְוָונִי.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «How does one smear» oil on «them?» He does so in a shape «similar» to «chi, and the rest» of the oil «is eaten» by priests. The Gemara asks: «What» is the meaning of: «Similar» to «chi? Rav Kahana said:» It is smeared in a shape «similar» to the «Greek» letter «chi,» Χ."
  }
